meta {
  name: Test Connection
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/settings/connections/test
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "id": "{{connectionId}}",
    "name": "QA PostgreSQL",
    "env": "QA",
    "type": "postgres",
    "host": "localhost",
    "port": 5432,
    "database": "app_core",
    "username": "dpilot",
    "password": "",
    "schema": "public"
  }
}

docs {
  Test a connection's values before saving them. Takes the Update Connection body (including `clearPassword` / `clearUri`), plus an optional `id` when editing an existing connection; omit `id` for a new one. Builds a throwaway client, runs the same trivial check as `GET /api/connections/:id/test` (`SELECT 1` / ping) within the usual 10-second connect timeout, and always closes it — the connection pools and the saved connection are never touched.

  With `id` and a blank `password` / `uri`, the stored secret is used only if the request passes the same gate as Update Connection (only `name`, `env`, `schemas` — and `schema`, except on Elasticsearch — may differ from what is stored); otherwise 400 "Re-enter the password…". An invalid body is a 400 like create/update.

  Returns `{ "ok": true }` or `{ "ok": false, "error": "<driver message>" }` (stored secrets are redacted from the message). Audited as `CONNECTION_TEST` with the connection id, env, type and outcome — never secrets.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
  **Admin only.**
}
